#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Runner for the scheduled L1 programmes (one backlog task per run).

Usage: ark-l1 [--program pii|dlp] SUBCOMMAND   (default: $ARK_L1_PROGRAM or pii)

Programmes share the clone, the cargo targets and the gate venv under ~/ark-l1; each keeps its
own state, stack, worktrees, dev data and holdout (pii: ~/ark-l1, dlp: ~/ark-dlp).

Isolation: the agent works in its own clone, never in a worktree of the shared repository.
Everything that executes agent-controlled code or reads agent-controlled git metadata (gate steps,
git status/bundle in the agent clone) runs in a systemd sandbox without credentials. Agent commits
reach the trusted repository only as a bundle; publish builds the "done" commit with plumbing in
the trusted repository and pushes from there.

Subcommands:
  next            restack the programme's open PRs, pick one task, create the agent clone; a rebase
                  that does not apply cleanly becomes the run's task (RESTACK:<branch>), resolved
                  by the agent, gated like any task and force-pushed with a lease by `publish`
  env             print the current run as shell assignments
  ahead           print the number of commits in the agent clone (sandboxed)
  gate            import the agent commits and run the independent checks (sandboxed)
  publish         mark the task done, push the branch, open a draft PR on the stack (idempotent)
  block ID REASON skip a task until `unblock`; drops the current worktree
  abort           drop the current worktree without blocking the task
  unblock ID      make a blocked task selectable again
  status          print stack, blocked tasks and the next candidate

Exit codes of `next`: 0 = task ready, 10 = nothing to do (reason on stdout),
11 = the previous run passed the gate but was not published yet (run `publish`).
"""

